Isoseq reads were generated from bacteriome tissue and residual body tissue (insects with bacteriome removed) from P. citri. Total RNA was extracted with TRIzol using manufacturer's protocol.

IsoSeq libraries were created from two biological replicates from each tissue type (bacteriome and residual body).

IsoSeq libraries were prepared using SMRTbell prep kit 3.0 (v02.2022). Pooled libraries underwent the PacBio binding and cleanup steps using the Revio Polymerase kit.

IsoSeq reads can be found under the following NCBI sample accession #s:
SAMN53396481 
SAMN53396482
SAMN53396479
SAMN53396480 

IsoSeq reads were trimmed using cutadapt (v5.1) and a custom python script (trim_polyA_sliding.py) using the isoseq_trim.sh script.

To extract IsoSeq reads originating from the mitogenome (and filter out nuclear, endosymbiotic, and NUMT sequences), BLAST was used to find reads with a high confidence hit to the assembled mitgenome (assembly_I5-EDIT_Final_cox1_start.fas) with the IsoSeq_mitogenome_BLAST.sh script.

These high confidence mitogenome reads were extracted from the complete IsoSeq read files using the extract_reads.py script.

Open reading frames were found in these reads using getorf (EMBOSS:6.6.0.0). 




